  "narration": "Silas leans back against the bar, one hand resting on the worn wood, and smiles in a way that doesn't quite reach his eyes. He watches the player with the practiced ease of someone who has spent years reading people.",
  "npc_response": "Call me Silas. I'm a thief, yes — but that's the polite version. The honest one is that I'm a finder. I've been around long enough to know that every tavern, every city, every locked door has a story worth stealing. And I've heard a lot of stories here. The bounty on Vane's head, the Marigold Venture's cargo, the door in the cellar that shouldn't be there... I've heard all of it. But the part I keep to myself? That's the part that makes me worth your coin. What do you want to know?"
