  "narration": "The priest shifts his weight on one foot, his gaze drifting toward the nearest jeweled coffin as if the stone itself might answer. His voice lowers, as though the walls are listening.",
  "npc_response": "This hall was built to keep the dead where they belong, and to keep the living from what they might do with the dead. Every coffin here holds a ruler who was once asked the same question you are asking now. Some came to claim their thrones. Others came to bury their names. The jewels are not for the dead — they are for the throne, and the throne is always watching. You may rest your eyes on the coffins, but do not read their faces. The dead do not speak, but the throne remembers every face that looked too long."
