  "memory_summary": "Vorn the Mad gives a manic, conspiratorial assessment of himself and the unraveling magic, heightening the player's suspicion.",
  "new_entities": [],
  "rule_flags": [],
  "narration": "Vorn the Mad paces in a tight circle, his eyes darting toward the raven-crowned tree as if expecting it to speak. He stops abruptly, one hand pressed to his temple, and lets out a low, delighted laugh that echoes strangely off the black stones.",
  "npc_response": "Vorn the Mad? *He* is a man who believes the stars are listening, and that the Silk Cloaks have been unmaking reality with their reckless rituals for years now. I am merely the one who noticed first. But you—wanderer with a blood-stained ledger and no name—do you know what it means when the magic unravels? It means the threads of everyone's life are fraying, and soon the pattern will be gone entirely. You should be careful. The ravens don't watch for sport. They watch because they know what happens when a thread snaps."
}

{
  "world_updates": [
    {
      "type": "NPC_SPOKE"
    }
  ],
  "memory_summary": "The player presses Hoakbera for a secret, and Hoakbera refuses to reveal one, instead offering a cryptic warning about the swamp's listening.",
  "new_entities": [],
  "rule_flags": [],
  "narration": "Hoakbera's eyes narrow, and the air around them seems to thicken, as if the swamp itself leans closer to listen. A low hum of unseen wings stirs the mist, and the fermenting goblins on the wall turn their heads, as if acknowledging the exchange.",
  "npc_response": "I have no deepest secret to give you, wanderer. The swamp does not keep secrets from those who ask in the right way—but you have not asked in the right way. You have asked with the hunger of a man who wants to be told what to do, not what to know. The bog does not answer to that. It answers to stillness, to patience, to a name you have not yet earned. I will not give you my secret, because the moment I do, it will be yours to carry, and I will not let it be carried by a hand that rushes."
}

{
  "world_updates": [
    {
      "type": "NPC_SPOKE"
    }
  ],
  "memory_summary": "The player directly accuses Hoakbera of hiding something and demands the deepest secret immediately.",
  "new_entities": [],
  "rule_flags": [],
  "narration": "Hoakbera's eyes narrow slightly, the green of his irises dimming as if the request itself weighs on him. He does not flinch, but his voice drops to a low, careful murmur, as though speaking too loudly might wake the swamp.",
  "npc_response": "I have seen the future, wanderer, and I have not told you what I saw. The water keeps its own secrets, and so do I. But you ask with your eyes open, and that is not how one asks a Hoakbera. Sit. Watch the reeds. Then ask again, and this time, ask with your heart, not your teeth."
}

