  "npc_response": "It was built for one thing: to hold the light. They say the chapel was raised when the sector was young, before the rains came and the names got lost. The walls were meant to keep the dark out, but the dark found its way in through the cracks. Now the roof is broken, the altar's gone, and the pews are just splinters. People still come. Not to pray. To stand in the light and forget. That's all this place is now. But the light doesn't stay. It leaks. And when it leaks, it shows what was always buried."
