  "npc_response": "You ask me about myself? I am the stitcher in the dark, wanderer. A needle where a god should be. But you want the truth, don't you? The truth is that I have no face worth showing in a mirror, because the mirror would show you what I am stitching into. The Silk Cloaks cut thread, yes—but I am the one who hears the pattern they are destroying. And you, with your blood-stained ledger, you are part of the pattern now. You should be careful what you ask of a man who knows too much. The ravens remember. And so do I."
}

{
