  "narration": "Vorn the Mad leans back against the twisted tree, his eyes darting toward the ravens as if they might answer. His fingers twitch at his throat, where he keeps a silver locket that pulses faintly.",
  "npc_response": "Me? I am the stitch that holds the wound together. The one who hears the god's name when the world forgets it. But that is not a secret — that is a curse. The secret is this: the ledger you carry is not yours, and the blood on it is not yours. Someone made you look guilty so the Silk Cloaks would have a reason to burn you. And yet, you still hear the silence between the ravens' cries. That means you are not what they think you are. That means you are the only one who can still hear what is unraveling. So tell me, wanderer — do you want to know what I am, or do you want to know what I have become?"
}

{
