  "npc_response": "I've been making arrows since before you were born, and I'll be doing it when you're gone. I don't have a name for myself beyond what the town calls me — the Fletcher. But if you want to know what I am, it's this: I'm the reason the garrison has arrows to shoot. I'm the man who watches the wood, the fletching, the string, and turns them into something that flies true. I don't keep secrets because I have none to hide. I keep them because some truths are meant to be earned, not handed over. But tell me — what do you want to know about me?"
