  "npc_response": "I was born with a crooked spine and a bent thumb, and I spent my first years learning to shape wood before I could read. I never went to war myself — I stayed here, in this shed, making sure that when the day came, the men who did would have arrows that flew true. Forty years, and I still check every shaft by hand. I don't trust machines to know what a good arrow feels like. But if you want to learn, you can watch me work. It's not a trade you take lightly — it's a promise you make to the ones who'll stand in your place."
}

