  "narration": "He sets down the half-finished arrow shaft and leans back against the rickety bench, his eyes drifting to the window where the chapel bell has just begun to toll.",
  "npc_response": "You ask about myself again, wanderer. I suppose I'll tell you what I've told the garrison. I was born with a crooked spine and a steady hand, and I learned to make arrows before I learned to read. The first time I sent an arrow through a practice target, it didn't fly straight — it curved, and it hit the bullseye anyway. That's the way it's been ever since. I've made arrows for every archer who's ever stood watch on this wall, and I've seen them fire when the night came. Some of them I know by name. The rest, I know by the way their hands shake when they draw. That's the truth of me, and it's all I've got to give."
}

{
  "world_updates": [
