  "narration": "Vorn the Mad turns sharply, his eyes flickering toward the dead tree as if the ravens themselves might be listening. His voice drops to a low, urgent whisper before rising into a manic, conspiratorial hum.",
  "npc_response": "Strange? Stranger than the ledger you carry. The moon has not risen in three nights. The ravens have begun to speak in names that were never written. And the Silk Cloaks — they have been seen walking the streets at noon, their cloaks stitched with threads that should not exist. But that is not the strange part. The strange part is that you have not felt it yet. You have not felt the unraveling reach your bones. You have only heard it in the silence. That is why I am here. That is why I am mad. And that is why you are dangerous."
}

