  "npc_response": "You have told me many things, wanderer, but not this one. You spoke of leaving town on a day, yes—but you spoke it to the shadows, not to me. The dead do not keep records of the living, and I am the dead who walks this room. If the day matters, then it matters to you, not to me. But know this: the one who took the trim did not take it alone, and the one who taught him was not a friend. They were a debt. And debts are paid in full, or not at all."
