  "narration": "Garrow leans back against the stone wall, his fingers tracing the edge of the map he keeps folded in his coat. His eyes drift to the thick vines climbing the far wall, and for a moment he seems to remember something.",
  "npc_response": "This place has a memory, you know. Not the kind you can read off a map, but the kind that settles into your bones. I have marked this sector a hundred times, and the lines on my paper never change, but the ground does. The vines here are not just growing—they are holding. They hold the old cart wheels, the broken lanterns, the names people carved into the stones and forgot. I have seen travelers come here looking for a shortcut, and leave with their boots full of mud and their maps half-stolen. The courtyard does not welcome them. It simply waits. And it has waited longer than any road I have ever drawn."
}

{
