  "narration": "Fenna leans back against the wet stone wall, one hand resting on a rusted railing. The water laps softly at the floorboards. He gives a slow, tired nod, as if the question is familiar.",
  "npc_response": "Long enough, friend. Longer than the garden's been quiet. I've kept this bridge watch for years—longer than most of the people who pass through remember the name of the place. I've seen the Gilded carts come and go, and I've seen the ones who don't come at all. The water's always been here. The quiet's new."
}

{
  "world_updates": [
    {
      "type": "NPC_SPOKE"
    }
  ],
  "memory_summary": "Garrow describes the courtyard's quiet decay and lingering shadows, offering a weary, observational account.",
